# Re-enforce KratosOS offline-mode radio silence when an rfkill device appears
# (finding R12-2). The two one-shot boot passes (kratos-firewall early, then
# kratos-offline-links after NetworkManager) can't cover a radio hotplugged
# LATER while the machine is still offline, which would otherwise come up
# unblocked. `kratos offline-links` is a no-op unless the saved mode is offline,
# and it takes the Kratos operation lock, so firing it on every rfkill add is
# safe. rfkill block is fast, so it won't be killed as a long-running udev RUN.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="rfkill", RUN+="/usr/local/bin/kratos offline-links"
